#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:2
msgid "Reviewing a pull request (PR) — how-to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:4
msgid ""
"All incoming code and documentation to ROS projects must be reviewed in a "
"pull request. This article explains how to prepare for and review a pull "
"request submitted by a contributor. After reading this article, you'll be "
"able to ensure changes in a pull request meet the required standards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:8
msgid ""
"**Area: contributing, community | Content-type: how-to | Experience: "
"beginner, intermediate, expert**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:12
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:15
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:17
msgid ""
"Reviewing a pull request (PR) from a contributor allows you to check that "
"their changes meet the appropriate guidelines and standards. Anyone is "
"welcome to review and approve a pull request. Changes are ready to merge "
"after they have been approved. Only a :doc:`Committer </The-ROS2-Project/"
"Governance>` for the target repository can merge a pull request into that "
"repository, and they will not do so until it has been approved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:23
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:25
msgid ""
"A code or documentation contributor has :doc:`made a pull request </The-ROS2-"
"Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Making-a-PR>` to merge their "
"changes into one of `the ROS repositories <https://github.com/ros2>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:28
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:31
msgid "1 Preparing for review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:33
msgid "Anyone is welcome to review a pull request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:35
msgid "A pull request generally requires two reviews before it can be merged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:37
msgid ""
"Treat reviewing a pull request as a collaborative activity involving the "
"submitter and other developers, rather than a passive or one-way process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:38
msgid "As a reviewer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:40
msgid ""
"You can make small improvements to code or documentation in-place, such as "
"fixing typos or addressing minor style issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:41
msgid ""
"You should make a best effort attempt to comment on the pull request within "
"one week of submission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:43
msgid ""
"When you begin reviewing a pull request, leave a comment to let others know "
"you are performing a review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:46
msgid "2 Reviewing the pull request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:48
msgid "Review the pull request against the following guidelines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:50
msgid ""
"Confirm the code or documentation changes are appropriate for the repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:51
msgid ""
"Verify the code is correct and complete, and scoped to a single, well "
"defined change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:52
msgid ""
"Check that the pull request targets the default branch (usually ``rolling``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:53
msgid ""
"If the changes are based on a design document, such as a `REP <https://reps."
"openrobotics.org/>`__, verify that the changes are consistent with the "
"design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:54
msgid "For code changes, ensure that the changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:56
msgid "Follow the :doc:`Developer guide <../Developer-Guide>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:57
msgid "Follow the :doc:`Code style guide <../Code-Style-Language-Versions>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:58
msgid "Include tests for the new feature or bug fix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:60
msgid ""
"For documentation changes, ensure the changes follow the :doc:`documentation "
"guidance </The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-To-ROS-2-"
"Documentation>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:61
msgid ""
"Confirm that the Continuous Integration (CI) run for the pull request passes "
"cleanly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:63
msgid "Provide your review comments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:65
msgid ""
"You can add review comments to the pull request for the submitter, or "
"suggest changes directly in the pull request (`see the GitHub documentation "
"for guidance <https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/collaborating-with-"
"pull-requests/reviewing-changes-in-pull-requests/commenting-on-a-pull-"
"request>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:67
msgid ""
"Follow these guidelines to make sure your review comments are useful and "
"actionable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:69
msgid ""
"Start with high-level comments (for example, asking for refactoring or "
"design changes), then move on to lower-level comments about specifics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:70
msgid "Consider providing the following types of comment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:72
msgid "**Positive feedback** — for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:74
msgid ""
"``Nice work on handling edge cases here — the early return makes the logic "
"much easier to follow.``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:76
msgid "**Questions** — for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:78
msgid ""
"``Just to make sure I'm not missing a requirement, is there a reason we're "
"using a custom sorting function here instead of localeCompare?``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:80
msgid "**Suggestions** — for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:82
msgid ""
"``You could simplify this loop using Array.map to make it more concise:``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:84
msgid "const names = users.map(user => user.name)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:88
msgid "**Issues** — for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:90
msgid ""
"``This function doesn't handle the case where response is null, which could "
"cause a runtime error — add a guard clause:``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:92
msgid ""
"if (!response) {\n"
"  return [...];\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:98
msgid ""
"**Housekeeping** — a change that isn't related to the main purpose of the "
"pull request, but helps to keep the repository healthy, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:100
msgid ""
"``Since this file is already being updated, could we also remove the unused "
"formatDate import at the top?``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:102
msgid ""
"**Minor details** — small, nitpicking details such as improving style or "
"readability, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:104
msgid ""
"``Minor naming suggestion; user_list could be named users to better reflect "
"that it's a collection.``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:106
msgid ""
"Be clear about what you expect to happen in response to each comment, "
"including whether the comment blocks merging the pull request, and whether "
"you consider your request optional or required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:107
msgid ""
"Remember to include positive feedback and thanks for the work done by the "
"submitter, and always be constructive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:110
msgid "3 Approving and merging the pull request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:112
msgid ""
"After you have reviewed the pull request and provided feedback, the "
"submitter may continue the discussion or iterate on their changes, adding "
"new commits to the PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:114
msgid ""
"When you are satisfied with the changes and they are ready to be merged, "
"approve the pull request (`see the GitHub documentation for guidance "
"<https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/collaborating-with-pull-requests/"
"reviewing-changes-in-pull-requests/approving-a-pull-request-with-required-"
"reviews>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:116
msgid ""
"Anyone is welcome to review a pull request, even if it already has a review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:117
msgid ""
"A pull request must have at least one approval, and in most cases, two "
"approvals, from a developer (other than the author) before it can be merged "
"to the target branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:118
msgid ""
"Only a Committer for the target repository can merge an approved pull "
"request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:120
msgid ""
"See the :doc:`current ROS Committers </The-ROS2-Project/Governance>` for the "
"list of people with merge permissions for the target repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Reviewing-a-PR.rst:122
msgid ""
"If the pull request has any dependencies, ensure that dependent pull "
"requests are merged in the correct order."
msgstr ""

